{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/03-turn-construction-recovery-cascade.md | sed -n '30,112p'\"","aggregated_output":"    30\t### Acceptance Criteria\n    31\t<!-- Jira: Acceptance Criteria field -->\n    32\t\n    33\t**AC-3.1:** When a component's derivation is `ready`, turn construction uses it directly.\n    34\t\n    35\t- **TC-3.1a:** Ready component used\n    36\t  - Given: a turn whose smoothed prompt is `ready`\n    37\t  - When: the turn is constructed\n    38\t  - Then: the smoothed prompt is used as-is\n    39\t\n    40\t**AC-3.2:** When a component's derivation is not ready (`pending` or `failed`, treated identically), construction attempts recovery and then falls through deterministic floor → original, always landing a usable component.\n    41\t\n    42\t- **TC-3.2a:** Pending recovers to floor\n    43\t  - Given: a turn whose smoothed prompt is `pending` and re-derivation does not complete\n    44\t  - When: the turn is constructed\n    45\t  - Then: the deterministic-cleaned prompt is used and the turn still constructs\n    46\t- **TC-3.2b:** Failed handled like pending\n    47\t  - Given: a turn whose smoothed prompt is `failed`\n    48\t  - When: the turn is constructed\n    49\t  - Then: the same cascade runs (no separate failed handling) and a usable component results\n    50\t- **TC-3.2c:** Floor unavailable → original\n    51\t  - Given: a component whose deterministic floor cannot be produced\n    52\t  - When: the turn is constructed\n    53\t  - Then: the original source content is used\n    54\t\n    55\t**AC-3.3:** A tool-result component never falls below its truncation floor during construction; it is never inserted raw/full as a fallback.\n    56\t\n    57\t- **TC-3.3a:** Tool result floored to truncation\n    58\t  - Given: a turn whose `tool_result_summary` is not ready\n    59\t  - When: the turn is constructed\n    60\t  - Then: the deterministic truncation is used, not the full raw result\n    61\t\n    62\t**AC-3.4:** Non-derived components (assistant text, assistant thinking, runtime-change blocks) are placed verbatim in the constructed turn.\n    63\t\n    64\t- **TC-3.4a:** Verbatim placement\n    65\t  - Given: a turn with assistant text, thinking, and a runtime-change block\n    66\t  - When: the turn is constructed\n    67\t  - Then: those components appear unchanged and in order\n    68\t\n    69\t**AC-3.5:** Turn construction never blocks on a derivation and never omits a component span; a not-ready derivation degrades, it does not stall or hole the turn.\n    70\t\n    71\t- **TC-3.5a:** No block, no hole\n    72\t  - Given: a turn with multiple not-ready derivations\n    73\t  - When: the turn is constructed\n    74\t  - Then: construction completes and every component is present as some rendering\n    75\t\n    76\t**AC-3.6:** Every component that fell back during construction is logged with enough detail to act on it: derivation type, subject id, why it floored (not-ready vs failed-floor), and which floor was used.\n    77\t\n    78\t- **TC-3.6a:** Fallback logged with detail\n    79\t  - Given: a turn construction where a smoothed prompt fell to its deterministic floor\n    80\t  - When: construction completes\n    81\t  - Then: a log entry records the derivation type, subject id, reason, and floor used\n    82\t- **TC-3.6b:** No fallback → no fallback log\n    83\t  - Given: a turn where all derivations are ready\n    84\t  - When: construction completes\n    85\t  - Then: no fallback log entries are written for it\n    86\t\n    87\t**AC-3.7:** Turn construction performs no provider work inside a DB write transaction.\n    88\t\n    89\t- **TC-3.7a:** Provider work outside transaction\n    90\t  - Given: turn construction attempts re-derivation of a not-ready component\n    91\t  - When: it runs\n    92\t  - Then: any provider call happens outside the write transaction that persists the turn\n    93\t\n    94\t**AC-3.8:** When turn-construction recovery resolves a not-ready component — by re-derivation, deterministic floor, or original-source floor — the resolved content is written back to the component's derivation record as `ready`, **except when a work item is still claimed or pending for that derivation**, in which case the record is left untouched (the floor is used in the rendering, but the in-flight worker is allowed to produce the real result). Persisted recovery outcomes land plain `ready`; there is no \"degraded\" state and no floor-used marker (no upgrade process consumes such a marker). The fallback *event* is logged; the canonical subject and any `ready` output carry no marker. A tool result's floor is deterministic truncation, never the raw full result.\n    95\t\n    96\t- **TC-3.8a:** Re-derivation lands ready\n    97\t  - Given: a `failed` component that recovery re-derives successfully\n    98\t  - When: construction completes\n    99\t  - Then: the derivation record is `ready` with the re-derived content\n   100\t- **TC-3.8b:** Floor recovery also lands ready\n   101\t  - Given: a `pending` component that recovery cannot re-derive, resolved at its deterministic floor\n   102\t  - When: construction completes\n   103\t  - Then: the derivation record is `ready` with the floored content, carries no degraded marker, and the fallback event is logged\n   104\t- **TC-3.8c:** Tool-result floor is truncation, never raw\n   105\t  - Given: a tool-result component whose summary is not ready and cannot be re-derived\n   106\t  - When: construction resolves it\n   107\t  - Then: the floor written back is deterministic truncation, never the raw full result\n   108\t- **TC-3.8d:** Write-back defers to live work\n   109\t  - Given: a not-ready component that still has a claimed or pending work item\n   110\t  - When: construction resolves it at the floor\n   111\t  - Then: the floor is used in the rendering but the derivation record is left untouched (not overwritten), so the in-flight worker still produces the real `ready` result\n   112\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
